rs/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Since this is a SceneDock warning, I think it will not cause spamming. As long as we're consistent, either approach is acceptable. It’s worth noting that the XR class enforces disabling FTI via setters rather than the constructor, so I predict this issue is highly unlikely to occur.\r\n\r\nHowever, I think we should standardize the behavior so that the warning is displayed even if the object isn’t visible. Since the SpringBoneCollision class is a collider, only the Gizmo is displayed and the mesh is not rendered, but the behavior of the SpringBone changes if SpringBoneCollision gets jittering.","created_at":"2026-05-17T10:53:00Z","updated_at":"2026-05-17T10:57:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119509#discussion_r3254498204","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119509","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3254498204"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119509#discussion_r3254498204"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119509"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/3254498204